  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Late summer surge of heat and humidity continues\nsevere thunderstorm and excessive rainfall threat through \nThursday\n\nA series of mid level impulses tracking eastward along the \nnorthern periphery of an expansive 500mb ridge will continue to \ninteract with anomalous moisture/instability and strong WNW flow\naloft to promote severe storm and excessive rain risk through\nThursday. \n\nAfter a round of severe storms this morning, robust \ndestabilization is occurring across western and central PA with\nplenty of heating and very rich dewpoints in the 70-75F range. \nMore thunderstorms are expected this afternoon through the \nevening in an convective environment highly supportive of\norganized storms capable of all severe weather hazards. There is\nalso the potential for heavy rain and flash flooding especially\nwere storms repeat over the same area. \n\nIncreased southwest to westerly flow on Thursday will push the\nwill continue to pump in the late summer heat and very high \ndewpoints. Heat advisory remains in effect from 11a-8p Thursday\nacross a portion of south central PA where max heat index values\nare projected to reach/exceed 100F.  \n\nThe severe risk will be focused more across the southwest\nquadrant of central PA Thursday, and south of the PA-MD border \non Friday. An upper trough passage favors one final round of \nshowers and storms on Friday, but fortunately the Labor Day \nweekend is trending dry. The upper ridge is forecast to \nretrograde by the end of the week which allows for a return to \nmore seasonal temperatures and lower humidity this weekend into\nearly next week.",
